diff --git a/packages/react-shell/CHANGELOG.md b/packages/react-shell/CHANGELOG.md
index bd3ab9e..beb7e03 100644
--- a/packages/react-shell/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/packages/react-shell/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.7.1
+
+Additive (#729, #755, #614, #426, #392, #174). Defaults render the same markup and CSS values as 0.7.0.
+
+- `Table` (typed columns, `rowKey`, caption, `empty`, `dense`, `striped`, `onRowClick` with Enter and Space, `selectedKey` as `aria-current`) and `Textarea`; classes `rk-table`, `rk-textarea` (#729). `Select` now takes `id`, `name` and `aria-describedby`, so a `Field` label can name it. Types `TableColumn`, `TableProps`, `SelectProps`.
+- `ModalShell`/`Dialog` `width` also takes a CSS length string, and `false` writes no inline width so a class can size the surface with `min()` or `clamp()` (#755).
+- `useShortcuts(defs, options?)` works without a `ShellProvider`: it uses the provider's registry when there is one, `options.registry` when given, and otherwise a private registry attached to `window`. New type `UseShortcutsOptions` (#755).
+- Class `.rk-hairline` (`--top`, `--bottom`) draws the `--rk-line-2` hairline as a border (#614).
+- `PromptDialog` is controllable: `value` and `onChange` (then `initialValue` is ignored); `requireValue` disables confirm while the text is blank (#426).
+- `ActionDialog` actions take `title` (tooltip). `ErrorBoundary fallback(error, reset, info)` passes React's `ErrorInfo` (`null` on the first fallback render, set right after). `ShortcutHelp` takes a plain `shortcuts` list (`{ label, chord, group? }`) and `platform` when there is no registry; `registry` is now optional. New `useAnchoredMenu(itemCount)` and `AnchoredMenu`: a button-triggered dropdown with roving focus, ArrowDown and ArrowUp on the trigger opening on the first or last row, Home and End, Tab and Escape closing with focus returned to the trigger, `aria-haspopup` and `aria-expanded` (#392).
+- `color-scheme` opt-out: the stylesheet sets `color-scheme: light|dark` on `:root`; put `data-rk-color-scheme="host"` on `<html>` to make it `normal` so the host's own value applies (#174). The caption cursor and outline tokens (`--rk-caption-cursor`, `--rk-caption-outline`, `--rk-caption-outline-offset`) shipped in 0.6.7.
+- Rejected here: a browser-preview mock data source (#383). A mock must never ship in release builds; it belongs in `@rightkit/qa`.
+
 ## 0.7.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 Additive, shipped in 0.7.0. Defaults render the same markup and CSS values as 0.6.8, except where noted.
